<v Jack Hitt>I found Allan also at his website, allanstern.net. He's been appealing his conviction for over 15 years. He makes the case that he's innocent. His argument is that the entire story of Sammy Feet and Crazy Joe and the explanation of the brother-in-law's murder and all the rest of it is hearsay, a grandiose fiction. In other words, Allan is saying, he can top us all. That he's the victim of the most outlandish Bob story ever told.
<v Jack Hitt>我也在他的网站allanstern.net上找到了艾伦。他已经对他的定罪上诉了15年多。他坚称自己无罪。他的论点是，关于萨米脚和疯狂乔的整个故事以及对谋杀姐夫的解释等等，都是传闻，是一种华丽的虚构。换句话说，艾伦在说，他能超越我们所有人。说他是史上最离谱的鲍勃故事的受害者。

00:26:27.550 --> 00:26:54.800
<v Ira Glass>Jack Hitt. He now lives in New Haven in a house, where he is his own super. He's also the co-host of the Peabody Award-winning podcast Uncivil. If you haven't heard it, seriously, give it a try. He's currently developing a new podcast. It's been many years since we first reported this story. In 2014, Allan Stern was released from prison. Bob, as far as we can tell, is no longer an elevator inspector for the city of New York. John Moscow is now practicing criminal law in Manhattan.
<v Ira Glass>杰克·希特。他现在住在纽黑文的一栋房子里，在那里他自己就是管理员。他也是皮博迪奖得主播客《Uncivil》的联合主持人。如果你还没听过，认真地说，试着听听看。他目前正在开发一个新的播客。距离我们首次报道这个故事已经过去很多年了。2014年，艾伦·斯特恩从监狱获释。据我们所知，鲍勃已不再担任纽约市的电梯检查员。约翰·莫斯科现在在曼哈顿从事刑事法律工作。

