<v Josh Bearman>He just thought that it would be a story that would amuse me, and he was absolutely correct. I guess he had no idea how successfully that story was going to appeal to me. And so, I mean, I kind of bought it. I mean, the idea of you lived to be in your middle ages, and you kind of never took any risks, and then things get totally-- the perspective refocuses in such a way that a weightlifting snowman makes as much sense as anything else. I kind of like it.
<v Josh Bearman>他只是觉得那会是一个让我开心的故事，而且他是完全正确的。我想他不知道那个故事会多么成功地吸引我。所以，我是说，我有点相信了。我是说，你活到了中年，你从未冒过任何险，然后事情变得完全——视角发生了如此的改变，以至于一个举重雪人就像任何其他事情一样合理。我有点喜欢它。

00:38:40.860 --> 00:38:45.640
<v Alex Blumberg>You kind of like it that he created a world in which it made sense to spend $30,000 on a weightlifting snowman?
<v Alex Blumberg>你有点喜欢他创造了一个花费3万美元在举重雪人身上变得合理的世界？

