00:45:17.870 --> 00:45:38.720
<v Ira Glass>So he sat down and he created a payment plan for them, a few hundred bucks every paycheck. But it was incredibly hard to make them stick to it. They had excuses. They couldn't do it. So he sat them down again, and they made up an agreement. And this time, they put it in writing. And then after month upon month of struggle-- it took over a year-- they finally paid it all back.
<v Ira Glass>所以他坐下来为他们制定了还款计划，每个发薪日几百块。但要让他们坚持下去极其困难。他们有各种借口。他们做不到。所以他再次让他们坐下来，达成了一项协议。这一次，他们把它写了下来。经过几个月的挣扎——花了超过一年——他们终于把钱全还上了。

00:45:38.720 --> 00:46:11.720
<v Dennis>Then things were OK for a while, but slowly but surely, started falling back into their own ways. And basically what I think it was the alcohol, basically. I remember vividly that she would come down to the laundry room. The laundry room was just outside the office. And she would go to the vending machine and buy can of pop after can of pop after can of pop.
<v Dennis>然后事情平静了一阵，但慢慢地，确定地，又开始走回老路。基本上我认为是酒精，基本上。我清楚记得她会下到洗衣房。洗衣房就在办公室外面。她会去自动售货机买一罐又一罐又一罐汽水。

00:46:11.720 --> 00:46:41.860
<v Dennis>And I always thought that was so weird. I was like, why is she buying, like, eight cans of Sprite or Coke when we're right next door to Walgreens, and she can just go buy a 12-pack? And I think what it was, was she was just getting Cokes to mix drinks with up in her apartment. I just remembered that being so weird.
<v Dennis>我一直觉得那太奇怪了。我想，为什么她要买八罐雪碧或可乐，明明我们就挨着沃尔格林，她可以直接去买一打？我想原因就是，她买可乐是为了带回公寓掺酒喝。我只记得那太奇怪了。

00:46:41.860 --> 00:46:58.230
<v Ira Glass>So Dennis watched and worried. He worried a lot. Anybody who knew Dennis that time would tell you. It was all he talked about. He'd go out with his friends, and this is what would be on his mind. What should he do? Was he being a sucker? What was going on with this couple?
<v Ira Glass>所以丹尼斯看着，担忧着。他非常担忧。任何当时认识丹尼斯的人都会告诉你。那是他挂在嘴边的话。他和朋友出去，这就是他心里想的事。他该怎么办？他是不是个傻瓜？这对夫妇到底怎么了？

00:46:58.230 --> 00:47:14.940
<v Ira Glass>It was the kind of worrying that you might expect from a family member or something. And of course, he was just the super, the property manager. And things got worse. At one point, another tenant found the wife passed out in the hallway of the building, lying there like she was dead, covered in vomit. Dennis ran to her side.
<v Ira Glass>那是你可能从家庭成员身上预期的那种担忧。当然，他只是管理员，物业经理。情况变得更糟。有一次，另一个住户发现那位妻子昏倒在楼道里，像死了一样躺在那里，身上全是呕吐物。丹尼斯跑向她身边。

00:47:14.940 --> 00:47:25.020
<v Dennis>And I was like, oh my God. What's wrong here? What happened to you? And she's just like, [GROANING]. She can't talk to me. She can't put a sentence together. She's just slurring all her words.
<v Dennis>我说，噢天哪。怎么了？你发生了什么？她只是，[呻吟]。她没法跟我说话。她连一句完整的话都说不出来。她只是口齿不清。

00:47:25.020 --> 00:47:38.010
<v Dennis>And so I was like, what do I do? I'm like, do I take her to the hospital? Do I call an ambulance? Like, well, what do I do? And anyway, she's like, I just need to go to bed. And so she was too drunk to basically open her door.
<v Dennis>所以我说，我该怎么办？我是说，我送她去医院吗？我打救护车吗？我该怎么办？无论如何，她说，我只是需要睡觉。于是她醉得基本上打不开自己的门。

